(2817849, 391186, 63104, '<td valign="top">I would have given this a higher score, but the eyes are very shiny, the flash has caught in them strongly for some reason</td>', 'I would have given this a higher score, but the eyes are very shiny, the flash has caught in them strongly for some reason', '2006-09-09 15:08:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2817862, 391242, 63104, '<td valign="top">with animals that have long faces, like dogs, depth of field is going to be an issue in any shot like this, because of the distance from the eyes to the nose. The solution is to tilt the camera so as to align the lens with an imaginary line joining the nose to the centre of the forehead ... or stop the aperture right down, which would mean the background wasnt as blurred, and would probably be too slow for something living that wants to move about.</td>', 'with animals that have long faces, like dogs, depth of field is going to be an issue in any shot like this, because of the distance from the eyes to the nose. The solution is to tilt the camera so as to align the lens with an imaginary line joining the nose to the centre of the forehead ... or stop the aperture right down, which would mean the background wasnt as blurred, and would probably be too slow for something living that wants to move about.', '2006-09-09 15:14:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2817870, 389737, 63104, '<td valign="top">it is a beautiful bird, but whatever you are shooting through (screen door?) is having a very obvious effect on the shot</td>', 'it is a beautiful bird, but whatever you are shooting through (screen door?) is having a very obvious effect on the shot', '2006-09-09 15:17:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2817875, 391324, 63104, '<td valign="top">its eyes are a bit soft. For a shot like this, where you know exactly what you want to be in focus, its worth selecting just of your autofocus points (if you have that facility) and pointing that at what needs critically to be in focus. Most cameras will let you select focus, then recompose.</td>', 'its eyes are a bit soft. For a shot like this, where you know exactly what you want to be in focus, its worth selecting just of your autofocus points (if you have that facility) and pointing that at what needs critically to be in focus. Most cameras will let you select focus, then recompose.', '2006-09-09 15:19:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2817881, 391486, 63104, '<td valign="top">nice shot, but the angle of the cigar seems a bit forced to get it into the frame. Come to think of it, the model doesnt actually look like he is enjoying the cigar that much.</td>', 'nice shot, but the angle of the cigar seems a bit forced to get it into the frame. Come to think of it, the model doesnt actually look like he is enjoying the cigar that much.', '2006-09-09 15:22:03.000000', NULL, 1),
