(2841402, 388063, 26906, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GeneralE:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by irakly:</b></div><hr/><i>For the members of the Critique Club: before you say something, please realize that some people know a thing or two about photography. It will help you avoid ridiculing yourself and looking as ignorant as the bloke who left his priceless thoughts under my last photo.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>&gt; This statement seems unnecessarily confrontational -- I find likely to divert the CC member''s attention away from your interesting photo, and to a consideration of your attitude, just as it has mine.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>oh, my comment was written in a context of a critique written to my previous photograph for a "stupid, stupid" challenge. your words seem to be much more adequate :) it is just my pesonal humple opinion that people must not be accepted to a critique club without screening. It seems like some people honestly believe that their words may help someone learn how to shoot better, but in reality they do nothing but harm to those who take their words for granted.</td>', 'Originally posted by GeneralE: Originally posted by irakly:For the members of the Critique Club: before you say something, please realize that some people know a thing or two about photography. It will help you avoid ridiculing yourself and looking as ignorant as the bloke who left his priceless thoughts under my last photo. > This statement seems unnecessarily confrontational -- I find likely to divert the CC member''s attention away from your interesting photo, and to a consideration of your attitude, just as it has mine.  oh, my comment was written in a context of a critique written to my previous photograph for a "stupid, stupid" challenge. your words seem to be much more adequate :) it is just my pesonal humple opinion that people must not be accepted to a critique club without screening. It seems like some people honestly believe that their words may help someone learn how to shoot better, but in reality they do nothing but harm to those who take their words for granted.', '2006-09-16 22:06:25.000000', NULL, 0),
